{"name":"Hibiscus Red","hex":"#a33737","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hibiscus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of the genus Hibiscus, especially Hibiscus syriacus, found in tropical to temperate regions, of some species used for making infusions/tea.","A cocktail made with champagne and cranberry juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hibiscus"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hibiscus","blocks":[{"text":"Hibiscus is a genus of plants in the family Malvaceae native to the tropics and subtropics. The genus is quite large, comprising 319 species. Hibiscus are renowned for their large, showy flowers and those species are commonly known simply as \"hibiscus\", or less widely known as rose mallow. The genus includes both annual and perennial herbaceous plants, as well as woody shrubs and small trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg/330px-Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus","wikidata":"Q157124"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/500px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/1280px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/500px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hibiscus tiliaceus in flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFou_-_sea_hibiscus_(Hibiscus_tiliaceus)_flower_and_leaf_(Niue).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Hibiscus_praeteritus_1DS-II_1-0988.jpg/500px-Hibiscus_praeteritus_1DS-II_1-0988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Hibiscus_praeteritus_1DS-II_1-0988.jpg/1280px-Hibiscus_praeteritus_1DS-II_1-0988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/